.UPDATE...
Issued at 1012 AM PDT Thu Aug 6 2026

Morning satellite looks a lot like Fogust - solid marine layer
covering all coastal waters and inland valleys. The depth this
morning per soundings and profilers is near 1800 feet. Latest
trends on satellite already show inland treat of the marine layer
back to the coast.

No update needed in the near term as the forecast is on track. A
slight warm up is on tap for today, especially outside of the
marine layer foot print.

Highlights for afternoon forecast package:

Fine tuning heat for Friday through Sunday. Still looking like the
weekend will be the hottest days and advisories will be issued
this afternoon.

Moonsonal moisture streams in from the south. Can
already see a few clouds over SoCal. Still not expecting a
convective threat for the Bay Area. Better forcing over the
Sierra.

Given the hot and dry set up fire weather conditions will return
to near critical for the weekend. Each afternoon will feature an
onshore push of breezy conditions.

