.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 1248 AM PDT Thu Aug 6 2026

Elevated fire weather conditions continue Thursday with hot and dry
conditions alongside the diurnal sea breeze. PSAs of Mid Coast to
Mendocino, Diablo/Santa Cruz Mountains, and Central Coast Interior
are all currently in the 97th percentile for ERC with Mid Coast to
Mendocino and Central Coast Interior forecast to reach daily record
values this weekend. This indicates potential for extreme burning
conditions. Even the more marine layer influenced PSAs of Bay Marine
and Central Coast are forecast to peak in the 80th-90th percentile.
Building high pressure will bring near-critical fire weather
conditions Friday through Sunday. Temperatures will be 10 to 15
degrees above normal with a shallow marine layer in place. Poor
minimum daytime relative humidity as low as 10% is expected in the
afternoons with little-to-no recovery expected overnight. The one
missing piece preventing this from being a Fire Weather Watch/Red
Flag Warning as of now is wind, it`s expected to be light. The
exception being through gaps/passes (namely Altamont Pass, the
Delta, and Pacheco Pass) and down the Salinas Valley. To add onto
this, the critical conditions are not expected to overlap spatially
(majority of a zone) or temporally (for at least 8 hours) to warrant
a product.

